  "body": "Stacked on #2969. Review the [open cutoff changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/a6e3a1310cae5f94df32b930c7e4a44da8b54845...980ed2af14fef01a6a1129ef973518563ed1d9ac).\n\nPost one straight open cutoff on a selected retained wall. Set left or right compensation from the operation. The ISO line is nominal. The native job uses separate entry and exit points beyond opposite faces of the stock. The post checks the approach, wire radius, rough offset and centered XY travel. This first cutoff process uses 20 mm stock.\n\nThe main cut separates the stock before the three trims. The operator must confirm that both pieces remain independently clamped through all passes. A separate confirmation locates the stock center at the midpoint of the machine travel. Both operation settings default to false when loading an older project. The existing capture setting can describe a catcher.\n\nRun either original example from the repository root:\n\n```sh\ncargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/cutoff-lower.camscript\ncargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/cutoff-upper.camscript\n```\n\nThe actual offline control ran four alternating traversals for both native sides. Each pass crossed the stock once along the 88 mm line. At a nominal Y of −6, the left cut measured Y −5.755, −5.845, −5.860 and −5.866 mm. The right cut gave the mirrored values about positive Y 6. All other cutting moves stayed in air. Both formal checks had zero job errors. The control requested machining and reference setup and reported option 131072. No physical cut was made.\n\nAll 16 scoped cutoff, die and native integration tests passed. The wire DTO test, 13 native post tests and all nine wire page tests passed, including Apply and Undo for the new fields. Strict Clippy passed for the app, motion, post and UI libraries. The before and after screenshots show the Passes page in the tested application.\n\n![Passes before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/5ec50c1daf4a1973250c2c14390e74ec97c8f870/before.png)\n\n![Passes after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/5ec50c1daf4a1973250c2c14390e74ec97c8f870/after.png)\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Native Agie wire posting supports a checked straight open cutoff in 20 mm stock. It requires distinct outside endpoints and explicit confirmations of clamping and stock placement.\n\nFixes #2962\n",
